ABSTRACT
The system uses the Unity3D engine to develop the Android app, and develop AR technology modules with Vuforia toolkit, integrating geographic information service technology and panorama technology. We combined the two tracking and registration methods which are based on sensors and natural images features, to implement a tourism navigation and AR introduction system based on Kulangsu, a famous scenic spot in Xiamen. The system is mainly divided into two modules, the route navigation module and the scenic spots guide module. Keywords: AR technology, Navigation System，Geographic information technology
1. INTRODUCTION
Augmented reality is a new technology developed on the basis of virtual reality. It combines computer graphics (CG), Space positioning technique, visualization technology and interactive technology. It enhances the real environment by superimposing computer-generated virtual objects, scenes or system prompts into real scenes, then it will provide users with a new sensory experience. In recent years, the hardware of smart phone has developed rapidly. It is an ideal platform to develop augmented reality technology because of the advantages of fast processor, multiple sensors, GPS, high-pixel built-in camera and large storage space. At home and abroad, there have been some attempts to introduce augmented reality technology into the outdoor and indoor navigation fields, and to enhance users' perception of enhancing information diversification
The combination of geolocation navigation technology and augmented reality technology is a major trend in current research: when augmented reality technology is applied to navigation, compared with the map and compass instructions, the walking route is marked directly on the screen through a three-dimensional model or icon, which is more intuitive and convenient, effectively guiding the user to the target location, avoiding problems such as not being able to read the map and distinguish the intersection.
This paper is about a development based on Android system, we used Unity3D engine to develop the app, used the Vuforia toolkit to develop augmented reality technology modules, integrated geographic information service technology and panorama technology. We combined the two tracking and registration methods which are based on sensors and natural images features, to implement a tourism navigation and AR introduction system based on Kulangsu, a famous scenic spot in Xiamen. The system is mainly divided into two modules, the route navigation module and the scenic spots guide module. The navigation module realizes real-time navigation by integrating the three-dimensional virtual tour guide into the real world scene, so that the user is more intuitive in the process of using the navigation, and can also make the user feel immersive. The scenic spots guide module can receive relevant information of the scenic spots through the AR application on the mobile phone, view the 3D virtual scenic spots model, and perform simple interaction.
2. RELATED WORK
