2.2 AR of tracking registration
Tracking registration technology is the basic technology of augmented reality, and it is the key to realize the seamless fusion of virtual information and real-life scenes. There are three main types of tracking registration technology for augmented reality systems: sensor-based tracking registration technology and machine vision-based tracking registration technology and hybrid tracking registration technology. Because of the variety of hybrid tracking registration technologies, we can take the combination of machine vision and inertial sensors, the combination of machine vision, GPS and a variety of sensors depended on the needs. The tracking registration technology adopted in this system applies two tracking registration methods based on sensors and image-based natural features
2.3 Sensor technology of Android system
Today's Android phones integrate many sensors, which are tiny physical devices that can be used to obtain data such as the operating status, placement direction, ambient temperature, and magnetic field strength of mobile devices. The Android system supports multiple types of sensors, including acceleration transducer, gyroscopes, magnetic field sensors, and distance sensors. In this article, we used acceleration transducer and magnetic field sensors to get the required phone orientation information. The sensor system can automatically report sensor accuracy and data change information to the upper layer, as well as provide some interfaces for setting sensor accuracy. These interfaces can be called in JAVA applications and JAVA frameworks
2.4 OpenGL ES
OpenGL ES is a standard for mobile graphics programming. It is simplified by the OpenGL 3D graphics API standard according to the characteristics of the mobile terminal. It is a 2D/3D graphics interface designed for embedded system development. In this article, the 2.0 version is used for 3D graphics rendering. Drawing an object through OpenGL ES on an Android system depends on its three-dimensional coordinate. We can map the sensor data matrix to the OpenGLES 3D coordinate system in real time, so that the objects drawn on the OpenGLES 3D coordinate system can simulate the operation effect of the mobile phone.
3. REQUIREMENT ANALYSIS
3.1 User requirements
Our system is geared towards self-tourists, who are our target users. After the initial research of the same type of application, many famous scenic spots in China have mobile applications to introduce attractions, such as the Leshan Buddhas scenic spot application, Sanfang Seven Alleys wisdom scenic spot, but also have a collection of scenic spot guide applications such as scenic spot treasure, but the promotion is extremely poor, the number of downloads on the application platform is less than 10,000 times, the star rating is even not shown because the number of evaluations is insufficient. Without consciously searching for scenic spots on the app platform, it's difficult for visitors to see such apps promoted locally at attractions. These attraction guiding apps are not functional enough to simply integrate the search engine's tour guides into the app, lacking a truly clear guiding function.
As an AR navigation system, the service group of the system is the tourists who come to Xiamen for sightseeing. At present, we focus on the functional development of Kulangsu, a national 5A-level tourist attraction in Xiamen. When visitors go to the island, they can see the QR code on the doorplates of many old buildings. You can see the corresponding introduction by using WeChat scanning. Therefore, for the Kulangsu AR navigation system, the early building introduction is the most basic user requirement of the system. In the process of self-help travel, there is no guide to plan the scenic spots to watch the route, and it is not convenient for the tourists to plan their own routes according to the network information. At this time, it is very important to combine the route planning and navigation system in the navigation system, and it is another key user requirement of our navigation system.
