3.2 Functional requirements The functional requirements of augmented reality navigation mainly include the following aspects: 1. The system can accurately locate the geographic location information of the user's current latitude and longitude coordinates, altitude, and interest. 2. The user can select or input the target attraction, and the system will plan the walking route for the user. 3. The user can start and terminate a certain navigation at any time. 4. The system can obtain the current real scene through the mobile phone camera, and the virtual elf in the mobile phone can guide the destination to the planned route in a virtual and real way. AR attraction introduction functional requirements include the following. 1. The user can choose the account login method to enter the system or directly enter the system without login. 2、 The system can accurately correspond to the three-dimensional model, text information and animation information according to the content of the marker. 3. The three-dimensional model and information can be decarded after being identified. 4, 3D model can be scaled, rotated and other ways to interact. 5. The system can use the attraction list to select different attractions to display information. 6. Each attraction should be introduced with text, panoramic interaction or AR model interaction.
4. DESIGN OF SYSTEM
Kulangsu AR Navigation System is currently a tourism system designed for Kulangsu travel with AR navigation, scenic spots introduction and panoramic display. There are two functional modules: the first module is the Kulangsu AR navigation module, which is used for route navigation between the scenic spots on Kulangsu Island; the second module is the AR scenic spots guide module, and the AR introduction of the scenic spots can appear by identifying specific areas. You can also view the 3D virtual panorama model and related information of the scenic spots at the same time. The core function of the AR navigation module is designed to use augmented reality technology to render the 3D route guide genie and road conditions after the user selects the target location and plans the route, and use the mobile phone sensor to make the guide genie change according to the change of the mobile phone posture, pointing to the correct direction in real time, giving users a more intuitive navigation experience. Figure 1 is a flow chart of the Kulangsu AR Navigation System。
