5. IMPLEMENTATION OF SYSTEM
This system uses the Unity platform and the Eclipse platform as the main development tool, and uses the GAD navigation development tool kit and the Vuforia augmented reality development toolkit to design and develop the multidirectional navigation system based on 3D model and 3D animation. 5.1 AR navigation module In the practice process of this system, one of the most important tasks is to obtain the location information. The system is developed on the Android platform, which provides three key API for the developer to implement location positioning, namely, Location Manager, Location Provider and Location. Location Manager can be used to get the current location and track the route of the mobile device. It supports two positioning methods, including GPS positioning and network positioning. In order to obtain the user's location information better, this paper uses these two methods to locate and obtain location information. The main difficulty of the AR navigation module lies in the visualization of navigation data. The method adopted in this paper is to convert the action identification information of the acquired road segment into a three-dimensional animation form to realize the navigation of the 3D virtual wizard tour guide in the real world. Based on this idea, this paper proposes a method to visualize navigation data.
