6. CONCLUSION
It is a valuable research direction to combine augmented reality technology with tourism navigation. This system uses the Unity3D platform for the overall development on the Android development environment, uses the Vuforia toolkit to develop the augmented reality technology module, and combines the geographic information service technology and the panorama technology. It combines the two types of tracking and registration based on the sensor and the natural features of the image, and studies and implements a famous viewspot on Kulangsu, Xiamen as the background of tourism navigation and AR scenic spot introduction system. After testing, the navigation module can obtain the positioning navigation information on the mobile devices, and realize the real-time navigation of the 3D virtual tour guide into the real world scene. Viewspot navigation module can receive the relevant information of the scenic spot through the AR application on the mobile phone, view the 3D virtual scenic spot model, and make a simple interaction. The system has initially completed the development of the basic functions of augmented reality navigation, allowing users to take a more visual tour on Gulangyu Island through the model animation in the screen. However, the current navigation module of the system still has areas for improvement. 1. the current three-dimensional model used for navigation is temporarily unable to identify the ground and create on the ground, the use of mobile phone gyroscopes in the virtual space orientation determination method is still defective, not yet used. 2. the three-dimensional model used for navigation can only be in front of the mobile phone lens and the user is a fixed distance away from the model that has not yet reached the desired goal has its own line of action. 3. the fusion of reality and reality is still not enough, the light mapping of the model still needs a complex implementation method, so as to distinguish the real world lighting situation in real time, and apply it to the rendering of the model.
